From b99d8c9e5ed09e267197d720a5df660becc79045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hang(Harry) Gao <GaohRyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:56:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] terrain: lifted references, foot clearance, scan inputs
 for world model / actor / critic, expanding checkpoint loader

- rewards: reference heights raised by the terrain (root and upper body by the mean terrain height under the robot,
  each foot by the terrain under its own reference position, knees half-way); velocity-weighted foot clearance term
  (imagination only); progress switch (default off). Flat ground: every term identical (checked on real states).
- world model: optional 187-d height scan input (zero-initialised columns), root height feature measured from the
  terrain under the root, base lift and ground lookup helpers, lifted termination features.
- policy: scan through a frozen pre-trained encoder (weights as buffers) or raw; critic: noise-free scan.
- terrain/expand.py: load a flat-ground checkpoint into the extended networks (new columns zero). Checked with the
  line G checkpoint: world model, policy (latent and raw) and critic outputs differ by exactly 0.0.
